@startuml

hide empty fields
hide empty methods

object discussion_thread {
    <<PK>> id: int
    open: bool
    created: datetime
    updated: datetime
    deleted: datetime
}

note left
discussion_thread is slated to be able to be
related to these existing discussion types:
• blog
• forum
• socialstream
• grades

and possibly new discussion types:
• assessment

These relation are expected to be via direct
foreign key relations, as opposed to a context
type and ID, as proposed earlier.

Relations to arbitrary content could be handled
by the revised `discussion_thread_context` table:
instead of a context type and ID, a URL reference
is stored.
end note

object discussion_post {
    <<PK>> id: int
    discussion_thread_id: int
    author_id: int
    content: text
    created: datetime
    updated: datetime
    deleted: datetime
}

object comms_news_article {
    <<PK>> id: int
    ...
    discussion_thread_id: int
}

object discussion_thread_context <<proposed>> {
    <<PK>> id: int
    discussion_thread_id: int
    url: url
}

object user {
    <<PK>> id: int
    username: varchar
    ...
}

discussion_thread -r-{ discussion_post : discussion_thread_id >

discussion_post }-r- user : author_id <

discussion_thread -d- comms_news_article : discussion_thread_id >

discussion_thread -d-{ discussion_thread_context : discussion_thread_id >

@enduml
